sentences.l:
He spoke, and upon the hilt of silver held his heavy hand,
and back into the sheath thrust the great sword, nor disobeyed
the word of Athena;

Yes, by this sceptre, which indeed never leaves and branches
will put forth, since it first left its stump on the mountains,
nor will it flourish again;

and now in turn it the sons of the Achaeans
in their palms carry, the justice-tending, who the rules of right
from Zeus keep;

and then you will not be able, though grieving,
to avail, when many by man-slaying Hector
dying fall;

and among them Nestor
sweet-of-speech sprang up, the clear-voiced speaker of the Pylians,
from whose tongue too, sweeter than honey, flowed the voice;

and for him already two generations of speech-dividing men
had perished, who earlier with him together were reared and born
in holy Pylos, and among the third he was lord;

But this man wishes to be above all others,
over all to hold sway he wishes, and over all to be lord,
and to all to give orders, which things some, I think, will not obey;
